@page "/mulligan-looting"

<PageTitle>Mulligan & Looting Calculator - Card Game Calculator</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Mulligan & Looting Calculator</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-6" Color="Color.Secondary">
    Simulate the London Mulligan rule and turn-by-turn card selection effects to model how quickly
    a multi-part combination is assembled in practice.
</MudText>

<MudExpansionPanels Class="mb-6" MultiExpansion="true">
    <MudExpansionPanel Text="Theory & Math">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Monte Carlo Simulation</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            Results are produced by repeated random simulation rather than closed-form mathematics.
            Each iteration plays one complete game sequence — shuffle, mulligan procedure, then turn-by-turn
            draws and card selection effects — and records whether all combo groups are assembled by the target
            turn. The reported probability is the fraction of successful iterations.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">London Mulligan Rule</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            On the \(k\)-th mulligan (\(k \geq 1\)), the player draws 7 cards, then places exactly \(k\)
            of them on the bottom of the library face-down, keeping a hand of \(7 - k\) cards.
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ \text{Hand size after } k \text{ mulligans} = 7 - k $$
        </div>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Some multiplayer formats (such as Commander) grant a <em>free first mulligan</em> — the first
            mulligan does not reduce hand size. When enabled, the formula becomes:
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ \text{Hand size (free first)} = 7 - \max(k - 1,\, 0) $$
        </div>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            The simulator takes a mulligan whenever the current hand does not contain at least one card
            from every required group, up to the configured maximum mulligan count.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Card Selection Effects</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            A card selection effect on turn \(T\) draws \(d\) cards then discards \(d\) cards. The simulator uses
            a <em>greedy keep policy</em>: when choosing which cards to discard, it retains cards that
            contribute to unfulfilled combo groups and discards excess copies and off-group cards first.
            This models optimal play rather than random discard.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-2">Wilson Score Confidence Interval</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Each reported probability is accompanied by a confidence interval computed using the
            Wilson score method, which remains accurate even when the probability is near 0% or 100%.
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ \text{CI} = \frac{\hat{p} + \dfrac{z^2}{2n} \pm z\,\sqrt{\dfrac{\hat{p}(1-\hat{p})}{n} + \dfrac{z^2}{4n^2}}}{1 + \dfrac{z^2}{n}} $$
        </div>
        <MudText>
            where \(\hat{p}\) is the empirical probability, \(n\) is the number of iterations, and \(z\) is
            the standard normal quantile for the chosen confidence level (e.g. \(z = 1.96\) for 95%).
        </MudText>
    </MudExpansionPanel>

    <MudExpansionPanel Text="How to Use">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Define the deck size, combo groups, and any card selection effects, then press
            <strong>Run Simulation</strong>. When card selection effects are present, the chart shows two lines —
            the base curve (no effects) and the card selection curve — letting you directly measure the
            improvement from each effect.
        </MudText>

        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Dense="true" Class="mb-4">
            For Commander games, enable the <strong>Free first mulligan</strong> checkbox before running.
            Press <strong>Reset to chosen format</strong> with 100-card Singleton selected to apply this
            setting automatically alongside the correct deck size.
        </MudAlert>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Comparing Base vs. Card Selection</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            Your 60-card combo deck has three groups: two 8-card groups and one 12-card group,
            each requiring at least 1 copy. You play Faithless Looting on turn 1 (draw 2, discard 2).
            How much does it improve your odds of having the combo assembled by turn 3?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Deck Size: <strong>60</strong>, Max Mulligans: <strong>3</strong></li>
            <li>Configure three groups matching your combo pieces</li>
            <li>Add card selection effect: Name <strong>Faithless Looting</strong>, Turn <strong>1</strong>, Draw <strong>2</strong>, Discard <strong>2</strong></li>
            <li>Max Turn: <strong>5</strong>, Iterations: <strong>1 000</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            Press <strong>Run Simulation</strong>. The orange <em>With card selection</em> line shows the
            improvement over the blue <em>Base</em> line — the gap at each turn quantifies how much
            Faithless Looting helps your consistency.
        </MudText>

        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" Dense="true">
            Increasing the iteration count narrows the confidence interval at the cost of longer run time.
            1 000 iterations is suitable for quick estimates; 10 000+ gives a margin of error below ±1.5% at 95% confidence.
        </MudAlert>
    </MudExpansionPanel>
</MudExpansionPanels>

<MudGrid>
    <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Parameters</MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudGrid Spacing="2" Class="mb-5">
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_deckSize" Label="Deck Size" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="7" Max="999" HelperText="Total cards (N)" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_maxMulligans" Label="Max Mulligans" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="0" Max="6" HelperText="London Mulligan" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="12">
                        <MudCheckBox @bind-Value="_freeFirstMulligan" Label="Free first mulligan" Color="Color.Primary" />
                    </MudItem>
                </MudGrid>

                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Card Groups</MudText>

                @foreach (var group in _groups)
                {
                    <MudGrid Spacing="1" Class="mb-1">
                        <MudItem xs="5">
                            <MudTextField @bind-Value="group.Name" Label="Name"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="3">
                            <MudNumericField @bind-Value="group.CopiesInDeck" Label="In Deck"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="@_deckSize" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="3">
                            <MudNumericField @bind-Value="group.DesiredCopies" Label="Want"
                                Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="@group.CopiesInDeck" />
                        </MudItem>
                        <MudItem xs="1" Class="d-flex align-center justify-center">
                            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Delete" Color="Color.Error"
                                Size="Size.Small" OnClick="@(() => RemoveGroup(group))" />
                        </MudItem>
                    </MudGrid>
                }

                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Primary" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add"
                    OnClick="AddGroup" Class="mt-2 mb-5">
                    Add Group
                </MudButton>

                <MudDivider Class="mb-4" />
                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-3">Simulation Settings</MudText>

                <MudGrid Spacing="2">
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_maxTurn" Label="Max Turn" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="1" Max="20" HelperText="Turns to simulate" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_iterations" Label="Iterations" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="1000" Max="1000000" Step="10000" />
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="6">
                        <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_confidenceLevel" Label="Confidence %" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                            Min="50" Max="99" />
                    </MudItem>
                </MudGrid>

                @if (_validationError is not null)
                {
                    <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" Class="mt-3" Dense="true">@_validationError</MudAlert>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
            <MudCardActions Class="flex-column align-start px-4 pb-4">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" OnClick="RunSimulation"
                    FullWidth="true" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.PlayArrow"
                    Disabled="_simulationRunning" Class="mb-2">
                    Run Simulation
                </MudButton>
                <MudTooltip Text="Resets Deck Size and the Free First Mulligan setting to the defaults of the currently selected format. Clears simulation results.">
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="ResetToFormat" FullWidth="true"
                        StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.RestartAlt">
                        Reset to chosen format
                    </MudButton>
                </MudTooltip>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mt-2"
                    Style="@(_simulationRunning ? "visibility: visible;" : "visibility: hidden;")">
                    Simulating&hellip; this may take a few seconds.
                </MudText>
            </MudCardActions>
        </MudCard>
    </MudItem>

    <MudItem xs="12" md="8">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Card Selection Effects</MudText>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                        Draw-discard effects applied on the specified turn
                    </MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                @if (_lootingEffects.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-2">
                        No card selection effects defined. The simulation will run without card selection.
                    </MudText>
                }
                else
                {
                    @foreach (var effect in _lootingEffects)
                    {
                        <MudGrid Spacing="1" Class="mb-1">
                            <MudItem xs="4">
                                <MudTextField @bind-Value="effect.Name" Label="Name"
                                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" />
                            </MudItem>
                            <MudItem xs="2">
                                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="effect.Turn" Label="Turn"
                                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="1" Max="@_maxTurn" />
                            </MudItem>
                            <MudItem xs="2">
                                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="effect.DrawCount" Label="Draw"
                                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="10" />
                            </MudItem>
                            <MudItem xs="2">
                                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="effect.DiscardCount" Label="Discard"
                                    Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense" Min="0" Max="10" />
                            </MudItem>
                            <MudItem xs="2" Class="d-flex align-center justify-center">
                                <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Delete" Color="Color.Error"
                                    Size="Size.Small" OnClick="@(() => RemoveLootingEffect(effect))" />
                            </MudItem>
                        </MudGrid>
                    }
                }
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Primary" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Add"
                    OnClick="AddLootingEffect" Class="mt-2">
                    Add Effect
                </MudButton>
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>

        @if (_simulated)
        {
            <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mt-4">
                <MudCardHeader>
                    <CardHeaderContent>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Probability of Assembly by Turn</MudText>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                            Cumulative — @_iterations.ToString("N0") iterations,
                            @_confidenceLevel% confidence, up to @_maxMulligans mulligans
                        </MudText>
                    </CardHeaderContent>
                </MudCardHeader>
                <MudCardContent>
                    <PlotlyChart Config="_chartConfig" Layout="_chartLayout" Data="_chartData" @ref="_chart" />
                </MudCardContent>
            </MudCard>
        }
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>
